<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dima Hasao</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as North Cachar Hills</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dima Hasao, until 2010 called the North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cachar">Cachar</a> Hills, is a hill district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with its headquarters at Haflong. It is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dimasa-people">Dimasa people</a>, whose kings ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maibang">Maibang</a> in the 16th to 18th centuries. The district has autonomous status under the Indian constitution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dima-hasao.jpg" alt="Dima Hasao" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xianhuns2020 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barail_Range_in_Dima_Hasao_district.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
